    "narrative": "For tonight\u2019s slate, **James Wood** (76.28) and **Mickey Moniak** (75.98) anchor our lineup, representing our highest-upside plays. **James Wood** benefits from an elite matchup against Young, whose 4.76 xERA provides a clear target, and the massive park factor boost (+16%) elevates him to our top spot in the order. Similarly, **Mickey Moniak** is in a prime position to capitalize on Paredes' shaky 5.42 xERA. His +19% SP skill boost and +14% platoon edge make him an essential start, particularly as we look to capitalize on his ability to drive in runs in a favorable environment. \n\nWhile **Josh Naylor** (66.96) and **Jose Caballero** (66.07) are solid core options, **Jose Caballero** remains particularly intriguing due to his high-leverage utility. Despite a slight penalty against the SP, he earns a +13% platoon edge and a +2% speed boost for his ability to capitalize on Bennett\u2019s slow delivery, keeping him in the mix for valuable stolen bases\u2014the most scarce asset in our 5x5 format. On the bench, **Cole Young** was the closest call for inclusion (44.73); while his speed profile is enticing, his placement in the #8 hole significantly hampered his efficiency score, ultimately keeping him behind the more consistent production we expect from **Zach McKinstry** and **Kyle Karros**.\n\nWe must remain cautious of the volatility at the bottom of the order. **Dalton Rushing** (40.69) and **Austin Riley** (46.71) are currently operating at a marginal level. **Austin Riley** in particular faces a tough test against Webb, whose 3.50 xERA is daunting, though he receives a rare +5% wind-out factor that keeps him above the bench floor. We are keeping a close eye on the weather and any late adjustments to the lineup configurations, as the margin for error remains thin when balancing these daily caps against the high performance requirements of our roster.",
